  "limits": "Screen of the study twin (1 scan unit = 1 mm by owner instruction, no physical calibration; 12% of its area is hypothesis closure, and the enclosed voids and thin handles in the unobserved regions are winding-number artefacts as much as geometry). Only six axis-aligned orientations are measured; tilted orientations are not. The 45 degree rule and the air-column volume are conventions, not a support design: no support type, density, tooth, removal access, heat path, recoater load or distortion is considered, short bridges are not credited, and the plate touches the lowest point without machining stock. Column volumes are envelope volumes, not support material. The strict flood fill lets powder leave through a 0.25 mm opening; the ball probe is the sensitivity to that. Attached studs are excluded from the body. Nothing here establishes printability, an orientation choice, a material, dimensional accuracy or function."
